Finite automata used as carry languages
========================================================================================
fibbinary DFA, bits read left-to-right after leading 1
  state Z(last bit 0/start): 0->Z, 1->O
  state O(last bit 1):       0->Z, 1->DEAD
  accepted states: Z,O

Moser-de Bruijn DFA, bits read least-significant first
  state E(even bit position): 0->O, 1->O
  state O(odd bit position):  0->E, 1->DEAD
  accepted states: E,O after at least one 1
  note: this language is a strict sparse sublanguage of fibbinary.

