Readout:
  * Fibbinary and Moser transversals can restore the mod-14 one-hole support,
    but their exact M values are strict, so the automata do not create new
    tight atoms in this scout.
  * Moser is a useful negative-control: it is extremely finite-state and
    no-carry, yet too magnitude-lacunary to preserve the LRC14 boundary.
  * The largest-safe-component column is the circle analogue of the
    large-stick/potato geometry prompt: it is exact and predicate-preserving.

